==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|avec|lang=frm}}, {{term|avecques||with|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|avoc|lang=fro}}, {{term|avoec|lang=fro}}, {{term|avuec||with|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} form of what would be *apud hŏque<ref name=a>http://www.cnrtl.fr/etymologie/avec</ref> in {{etyl|la|fr}} ({{term|apud||with, near, close to|lang=la}} + {{term|hoc|lang=la}} + {{term|-que|lang=la}}).  Used as a replacement for {{la}} {{term|cum||with|lang=la}} in [[w:Merovingian|Merovingian]] and [[w:Carolingian|Carolingian]] documents. Gradually supplanted Old French {{term|od||with|lang=fro}}, itself from ''apud''.<ref name=a/>

